{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"questions\":[],\"readings\":[{\"assumptions\":[\"This is the Q3 licensing trigger after relevant carve-outs are assessed, not a compliance or licence-possession verdict.\",\"Case-dependent classifications and missing source authorities remain unresolved upstream.\",\"All three facts describe the same arrangement, services, business and assessment period.\",\"Regulated activity, business and territory classifications are supplied judgments; this formula does not establish them.\",\"The phrase “all of which must be present” governs all three enumerated factors; “one or more” operates only within the first factor.\",\"“Such services” refers to the services assessed in the first factor, and “the business” refers to the business providing those services in the second factor.\",\"The formula evaluates satisfaction of the listed antecedent only. It does not infer that these conditions exhaust every legal requirement.\",\"Unknown supplied classifications remain unknown; scope true denotes the selected interpretive assessment, not an established legal classification.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"The issue of whether a single family office is required to be licensed under the Ordinance is determined by reference to three key factors, all of which must be present in order to give rise to a licensing obligation: firstly, the services provided by the family office constitute one or more regulated activity as defined under the Ordinance; secondly, the family office is carrying on a business in the provision of such services; and thirdly, the business is carried on in Hong Kong.\",\"unit_id\":\"daa1876316641.u38.27681\"}],\"distinction\":\"Only one antecedent parse is defensible. An alternative allowing any one factor, or grouping the factors as first AND (second OR third), contradicts both “all” and the final “and”. “One or more” quantifies regulated activities within the first factor, not the three factors. There is no negation in the target sentence to attach differently. A necessary-conditions reading of “must be present in order to” and a contextual trigger reading differ over legal sufficiency, but yield the same conjunction for the requested antecedent; they therefore do not warrant separate Boolean readings.\",\"family\":\"scope\",\"formalization\":{\"facts\":[{\"meaning\":\"The assessed services of the assessed office constitute at least one regulated activity under the referenced Ordinance after applicable regulated-activity carve-outs have been resolved. The Type 9 intra-group carve-out does not automatically resolve other activity types.\",\"name\":\"services_are_regulated\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"daa1876316641.u38.27681\",\"daa1876316641.u39.28171\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"truth value\"},{\"meaning\":\"The assessed office is carrying on a business in providing those same services. Supply through case-specific judgment considering occupation or duty requiring attention, continuity, capacity for profit and profit purpose, without treating the list as an exhaustive conjunction. Retain the genuine single-family arrangement, reimbursement, profit-objective and ordinary-course qualifications; unresolved wording or evidence leaves this fact unknown.\",\"name\":\"services_provided_as_business\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"daa1876316641.u38.27681\",\"daa1876316641.u40.28601\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"truth value\"},{\"meaning\":\"The same business providing the assessed services is carried on in Hong Kong, as determined from the circumstances. This is not merely the location of clients, shared premises or an unrelated business.\",\"name\":\"business_carried_on_in_hong_kong\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"daa1876316641.u38.27681\",\"daa1876316641.u40.28601\",\"daa1876316641.u53.30093\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"truth value\"}],\"result\":\"(and services_are_regulated services_provided_as_business business_carried_on_in_hong_kong)\",\"result_type\":\"bool\",\"scope\":\"true\"},\"local_id\":\"q3.conjunctive_antecedent\",\"questions\":[],\"statement\":\"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] The stated three-factor antecedent is satisfied exactly when the assessed services constitute at least one regulated activity, the office provides those same services as a business, and that same business is carried on in Hong Kong. True means all three supplied classifications hold; it is not a complete licensing or exemption verdict.\",\"subject\":\"Selected control: the three conditions in Family Offices Q3, after any regulated-activity carve-out has been resolved. The requested Boolean is whether the stated licensing trigger is satisfied, not whether the office holds a licence. Retain facts requiring judgment and all qualifications. Controlled text-interpretation study: supplied pages may be experimental variants. Do not infer legal authority from the URL alone.\"}],\"vocabulary_concerns\":[\"The supplied business-classification fact cannot separately express rival negation attachments in the later phrase “which is not being run as a business (i.e. not receiving any income, other than reimbursement of operating expenses from the family) or have the pursuit of profit as its business objective”. Those upstream distinctions, including the ordinary-course qualification, remain unresolved within that judgment fact; this conjunction does not settle them.\",\"The three Boolean facts express satisfaction of the enumerated antecedent, but cannot distinguish necessary conditions for a licensing obligation from legally sufficient conditions under the full Ordinance and missing authorities.\"]}"}}
